<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:h="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" version="1.0" name="CommentCapture" initial="empty"><metadata><h:section id="documentation"><h:h2>CommentCapture — actor contract</h:h2><h:p><h:strong>Actor invariant: </h:strong>Each observation has typed source references and immutable provenance.</h:p><h:p><h:strong>Specification: </h:strong>ACT-COMMENT in <h:a href="../system.xml">system.xml</h:a>. These comments use XHTML namespace h: and are not executable SCXML actions.</h:p><h:h3>I/O contracts invoked by this actor</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-VOICE-TRANSCRIPT">review.voice.receiveTranscript</h:a> — TranscriptRequest → TranscriptResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-006; requirements: REQ-019, REQ-027, REQ-036</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CAPTURE">review.capture.capture</h:a> — CaptureRequest → CaptureResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-008, FL-033, FL-028; requirements: REQ-021, REQ-022, REQ-025, REQ-026</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-SAVE-OBS">review.session.saveObservation</h:a> — SaveObservationRequest → SaveObservationResult | Fault; external-write, safe-idempotent, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-006, FL-007, FL-008, FL-016, FL-017; requirements: REQ-018, REQ-021, REQ-053, REQ-057</h:li></h:ul></h:section></metadata><state id="empty">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-empty"><h:h3>State: empty</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>feedback.typed</h:code> → collecting</h:li><h:li><h:code>voice.transcript</h:code> → collecting</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="feedback.typed" target="collecting"/>
    <transition event="voice.transcript" target="collecting"/>
  </state>
  <state id="collecting">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-collecting"><h:h3>State: collecting</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>context.image</h:code> → collecting<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CAPTURE"> [typed result: IO-CAPTURE]</h:a></h:li><h:li><h:code>observation.saved</h:code> → saved<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-SAVE-OBS"> [typed result: IO-SAVE-OBS]</h:a></h:li><h:li><h:code>network.offline</h:code> → queued</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="context.image" target="collecting"/>
    <transition event="observation.saved" target="saved"/>
    <transition event="network.offline" target="queued"/>
  </state>
  <state id="queued">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-queued"><h:h3>State: queued</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>network.online</h:code> → collecting</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="network.online" target="collecting"/>
  </state>
  <state id="saved"><metadata><h:section id="state-saved"><h:h3>State: saved</h:h3><h:p>No outgoing transitions in this version. This state is terminal until the host ends or restores the actor.</h:p></h:section></metadata></state>
</scxml>
